WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.162
A list is a content item that holds other content items, like a

00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:06.670
blog and its posts.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:11.014
In this video, you choose the types a list accepts, how many items

00:00:11.014 --> 00:00:14.030
each page shows, and the order of the items.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.203
A list is a content item with the List part, such as a Blog.

00:00:22.203 --> 00:00:26.426
Its items are content items of the types you choose, such as Blog Posts.

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:30.920
The settings sit on the content type, so every list of that type shares them.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:36.201
Contained Content Types chooses which content types the list accepts.

00:00:36.201 --> 00:00:40.188
Page Size sets how many items appear on each page, and it is

00:00:40.188 --> 00:00:41.940
10 until you change it.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:46.422
Enable Ordering lets you arrange the items by dragging them.

00:00:46.422 --> 00:00:52.530
Two display options, Show full pager and Show container's header, change what appears around the list.

00:00:56.763 --> 00:01:01.483
The List settings live under Design, Content Definition, Content Types.

00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:05.713
Each content type has an Edit button; let's edit the Blog type.

00:01:06.169 --> 00:01:09.759
In the Parts list, the List part has an Edit button of its own.

00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:12.049
Select it to open the part's settings.

00:01:12.509 --> 00:01:14.726
The List part has these settings:

00:01:14.726 --> 00:01:20.637
Page Size, Enable Ordering, Contained Content Types, Show container's header, and Show full pager.

00:01:20.637 --> 00:01:23.479
The next chapters change them one at a time.

00:01:27.695 --> 00:01:29.822
This is the admin page of a blog.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:34.185
Because the list accepts a single content type, Blog Post, one Create Blog

00:01:34.185 --> 00:01:35.875
Post button adds an item.

00:01:36.326 --> 00:01:41.162
Contained Content Types shows every content type of the site as a checkbox.

00:01:41.162 --> 00:01:43.790
Let's check Article as well, and save.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:46.716
Saving with no type checked shows an error.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.287
Back on the blog's page, a New menu replaces the single button.

00:01:51.287 --> 00:01:54.740
It lists both accepted types, Article and Blog Post.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.366
Page Size sets how many items appear on a page.

00:02:02.366 --> 00:02:06.402
At the default of 10, all eight posts of this blog fit on

00:02:06.402 --> 00:02:08.260
one page, newest first.

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:10.036
Let's set it to 3.

00:02:10.036 --> 00:02:15.107
Open the List settings, enter the number in the Page Size field, and save the settings.

00:02:15.566 --> 00:02:19.894
On the blog's admin page, the list shows three posts, with an arrow

00:02:19.894 --> 00:02:22.266
below it that opens the next page.

00:02:22.719 --> 00:02:25.266
The same setting applies on the site.

00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:30.419
Visitors see three posts at a time, and the Older Posts link opens the next page.

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:34.942
The second page adds a Newer Posts link to go back, next to

00:02:34.942 --> 00:02:38.629
Older Posts, which continues toward the oldest posts.

00:02:42.835 --> 00:02:46.633
Without ordering, a list shows its newest items first.

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:51.065
Enable Ordering lets you choose the order yourself, by dragging.

00:02:51.525 --> 00:02:53.581
Check Enable Ordering and save.

00:02:53.581 --> 00:02:57.803
Turning it on numbers the existing items from newest to oldest, so the

00:02:57.803 --> 00:03:00.525
list looks the same until you drag an item.

00:03:00.984 --> 00:03:05.204
On the blog's admin page, every row has a drag handle at its start.

00:03:05.657 --> 00:03:08.589
Open the second page with the arrow below the list.

00:03:08.589 --> 00:03:11.469
Let's drag its third post to the top of that page.

00:03:11.469 --> 00:03:13.937
The order is saved as soon as you drop it.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.508
Open the blog on the site, and select Older Posts.

00:03:17.508 --> 00:03:20.006
The second page follows the same order:

00:03:20.006 --> 00:03:22.060
the post you moved comes first.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.860
Items you create later are added at the end of the list.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:28.500
A post you create appears on the last page.

00:03:28.955 --> 00:03:32.230
Searching or filtering the list hides the handles.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.915
Search for garden, and the matching rows have no handles.

00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:43.409
Show full pager adds numbered pages to the pager.

00:03:43.409 --> 00:03:48.358
Its hint notes that it needs an additional database query to count the items.

00:03:48.358 --> 00:03:49.849
Check it, and save.

00:03:50.302 --> 00:03:54.534
The admin page then shows a number for every page, with arrows on

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:58.229
either side for the first, previous, next and last page.

00:03:58.229 --> 00:04:00.792
Select a number to jump to that page.

00:04:01.243 --> 00:04:06.278
Show container's header adds a card with the title of the list above its items.

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:09.063
Back in the settings, check it, and save.

00:04:09.513 --> 00:04:13.306
The card appears on the list's admin page, and on the editor page

00:04:13.306 --> 00:04:14.963
of each post in the list.

00:04:16.963 --> 00:04:20.900
That's how a list decides what it accepts, how many items a page

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.700
shows, and in which order.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.163
Thanks for watching.

